# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# www -> apex is NOT handled here. Tested against the live site on 2026-09-07:
# Cloudflare Pages matches _redirects on the PATH only, so a source with a
# hostname in it is silently ignored — www.builtbytyler.com still answered 200
# with its own copy of the page rather than a 301.
#
#   curl -sI https://www.builtbytyler.com/ | head -1    # HTTP/1.1 200 OK
#
# What holds the line in the meantime is the <link rel="canonical"> now in
# every page head, which www serves too, pointing at the apex. Google honours
# that and consolidates the two hosts. A 301 is still the stronger signal, and
# it has to be made in the dashboard:
#
#   Cloudflare > builtbytyler.com > Rules > Redirect Rules > Create
#     If  hostname equals  www.builtbytyler.com
#     Then  dynamic redirect  301  to  concat("https://builtbytyler.com", http.request.uri.path)
#     Preserve query string: on
#
# This file is kept because path redirects (an old URL moving, say) do work
# here and belong in it.
